    "description": "What: 'Field D', an enemy ANTI-TANK field (110-150, 50-110, a mine every 4 m), unknown to Friend. A Friend 'Walker' crosses it on foot from (70, 70) to (185, 70); a Friend M1 'Tank' drives across it from (60, 95) to (190, 95). An anti-tank mine needs a vehicle's weight: the man walks over it unharmed; the tank sets one off, is hurt from BELOW (the armour's Bottom facing), and its MineStrike drill stops it (CE-4624 MS-T1, MS-B1; Minefields MF-2, MR-10, MR-16). Judge: (1) the Walker gets across (x > 160) and is never hurt; (2) a mine goes off; (3) the Tank is hurt; (4) the Tank reacts MineStrike; (5) the Tank does not get across (x stays below 160). Not yet: followers reversing in the struck vehicle's tracks (R-2125, INTERIM until terrain's breadcrumbs). Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh mf-at-vs-vehicle"
  },
